==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gd|mga|alt}}, from {{inh|gd|sga|alt||shore, cliff}}, from {{inh|gd|cel-pro|*altos|t=cliff}}.

Cognates in the Celtic languages include {{cog|ga|alt||height, glenside, cliff}}, {{cog|kw|als||cliff}}, and {{cog|br|aot||shore}}. MacBain suggests the Scottish Gaelic form and meaning has a Pictish origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gd|/ˈauɫ̪t/}}

===Noun===
{{gd-noun|g=m|gen=uillt|pl=uillt}}

# steep-sided [[stream]]
#: {{ux|gd|Tha an t-'''allt''' a' ruith.|The '''stream''' is flowing.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|gd|alltan||burn, brook, stream}}
* {{l|gd|leth-allt||stream with one steep side, not two}}

